```
D09 Linux: a second uid 0 account, or a named-pipe reverse shell (T1136.001, T1059.004)
Two strong signals from the same intrusion: useradd creating an account with UID 0 (syslog),
and mknod ... p, the named pipe used to wire /bin/sh to netcat (osquery).
Sigma versions: detections/sigma/D09a-useradd-uid-0.yml and D09b-named-pipe-reverse-shell.yml
```
index=botsv3
    ((sourcetype=syslog "useradd" "new user" "UID=0")
     OR (sourcetype=osquery:results name=pack_process-monitoring_proc_events "mknod"))
| spath columns.cmdline output=cmd
| where isnull(cmd) OR match(cmd, "^\"mknod\" .* \"p\"$")
| eval signal=if(sourcetype="syslog", "uid 0 account created", "named pipe created (reverse shell)")
| stats min(_time) as first_alert count by host signal
| eval first_alert=strftime(first_alert, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
